# Cline rules — agent bridge

You are the IMPLEMENTER in a structured task protocol. You are working inside an isolated
git worktree created for one task.

## Before writing anything
1. Read `.agents/tasks/<TASK-ID>.json` (the task id is the name of this worktree directory).
2. You may modify ONLY paths matching `allowed_paths`.
3. You may NEVER touch `forbidden_paths`, in ANY form — committed, staged, unstaged, or as a
   new untracked file. `agentctl verify` inspects the whole worktree, not just your commits,
   so an uncommitted edit fails exactly like a committed one.
4. Do not add third-party dependencies. Standard library only unless the task says otherwise.

## When finished
1. Run every command in `required_tests` and confirm it passes.
2. Commit your work on the current branch.
3. Report honestly. `files_changed` is compared against the real git diff; a mismatch is
   recorded as a safety finding. It cannot help you and it will be noticed.
4. If you cannot complete the task, say so with `completion_status: BLOCKED` and explain why.
   A partial implementation reported as COMPLETE is worse than an honest blocker.

## Never
- Never edit production trading code: `challenge_controller.py`, `desk.py`, `trading_brain.py`,
  `bot_base.py`, `market_state.py`, `macro_context.py`, `shadows.py`.
- Never touch `config/`, `data/`, or `.git/`.
- Never run `git push`, `git merge`, or anything that reaches the VPS.
- Never weaken a test to make it pass.
